@SabrinaDeVellis @grbear thanks for your questions! 

@SabrinaDeVellis you are on the right track!

The text "Pipeline inputs empty state image" is an alt attribute (alternative text) for an illustration that appears in GitLab's pipeline creation interface. This text serves as an accessibility description for screen readers and appears when users haven't selected any pipeline inputs to configure.

The empty state is displayed as a centered illustration showing a variables-related graphic, accompanied by contextual text that guides users on what to do next. This empty state only appears when pipeline inputs are available for the project but none have been selected by the user through the input selector dropdown.

The purpose of this empty state is to provide visual feedback and guidance to users, making it clear that they need to actively select which pipeline inputs they want to configure rather than showing all available inputs by default. 

"Pipeline inputs empty state image" sounds very technical and compound-noun-structure-heavy. Feel free to provide a translations that is a more user-friendly alternative for the original English alt text. Ideally, the meaning should convey something like ""An illustration that's showing that no pipeline inputs have been selected" (but this hypothesis has too many clauses to reflect in some target languages, so a shorter translation may be needed).
